From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 20:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: prefer installed calibration to the nvmem cell

The Arista C-360 dual 5 GHz plan installs calibration from ART 0x71800,
while its device tree names the default 6 GHz plan at 0x1000. Read an
already installed cal-<bus>-<device>.bin directly before trying nvmem.
Keep the existing nvmem and firmware-helper fallbacks when it is absent.

Adapted from openwrt-arista main/files 960-wifi-ath11k-calibration-file-
before-nvmem.patch at 1d5314147cfa375fd8224bfc25b3deea26c0d8c3.

Signed-off-by: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/qmi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/qmi.c
@@ -2615,6 +2615,7 @@ static int ath11k_qmi_load_bdf_qmi(struc
 {
 	struct device *dev = ab->dev;
 	char filename[ATH11K_QMI_MAX_BDF_FILE_NAME_SIZE];
+	char path[100];
 	struct ath11k_board_data bd;
 	u32 fw_size, file_type;
 	const struct firmware *fw_entry = NULL;
@@ -2662,6 +2663,20 @@ static int ath11k_qmi_load_bdf_qmi(struc
 		fw_size = ATH11K_QMI_MAX_BDF_FILE_NAME_SIZE;
 	} else {
 		file_type = ATH11K_QMI_FILE_TYPE_CALDATA;
+
+		/* A radio plan may install calibration from a different ART
+		 * cell before probe. Prefer that file to the default nvmem cell.
+		 */
+		snprintf(filename, sizeof(filename), "cal-%s-%s.bin",
+			 ath11k_bus_str(ab->hif.bus), dev_name(dev));
+		ath11k_core_create_firmware_path(ab, filename, path, sizeof(path));
+		if (!request_firmware_direct(&fw_entry, path, dev)) {
+			ath11k_dbg(ab, ATH11K_DBG_QMI,
+				   "calibration data from %s before nvmem\n", path);
+			goto success;
+		}
+		fw_entry = NULL;
+
 		ret = ath11k_qmi_get_caldata_nvmem(ab, &caldata, &fw_size);
 		if (!ret) {
 			tmp = caldata;
